      "front": "Figure skating: Why does a skater spin faster when pulling in their arms?",
      "back": "Without external torque, angular momentum is conserved: \n$L = I\\omega = \\text{constant}$\nWhen pulling the arms in, $I$ decreases, so $\\omega$ increases. The skater performs muscular work; this increases rotational energy $E_\\text{rot}= \\frac12 I \\omega^2$\nMnemonic: When pulling the arms in, angular momentum remains conserved, rotational energy increases.",
